Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) Custom Roles Documentation
Overview

In AKS, permissions can be segregated into Control Plane, Data Plane, and Reader roles to ensure secure and structured access management:

AKS Control Plane Admin – Full cluster-level control including namespace creation and cluster-wide resource management.

AKS Data Plane Admin – Namespace-level workload management; cannot create or manage cluster-wide resources.

AKS Reader Role – Read-only access to view cluster and namespace resources; cannot modify or create resources.

1. AKS Control Plane Admin

Description:
This role provides full administrative control over the AKS cluster, including namespace creation, RBAC management, and all cluster-level and workload resources.

Scope: Cluster-level (assignable per cluster)

Permissions (JSON example):

{
  "roleName": "AKS Control Plane Admin",
  "description": "Full cluster admin permissions including namespaces, RBAC, and cluster resources.",
  "assignableScopes": ["/subscriptions/<subscription-id>/resourceGroups/<rg>/providers/Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/<cluster>"],
  "permissions": [
    {
      "actions": [
        "Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/*",
        "Microsoft.Authorization/*/read",
        "Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups/read"
      ],
      "notActions": [],
      "dataActions": ["Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/*"],
      "notDataActions": []
    }
  ]
}


Capabilities:

Resource / Action	Allowed?	Notes
Namespaces	✅ Create / Update / Delete	Cluster-level operation
ClusterRoles / ClusterRoleBindings	✅ Manage	Full control over RBAC
Deployments / Pods	✅ Full control	Across all namespaces
Services / ConfigMaps / Secrets	✅ Full control	Across all namespaces
Ingress / StatefulSets / DaemonSets / Jobs / CronJobs	✅ Full control	Across all namespaces
ResourceQuotas / LimitRanges	✅ Full control	Across all namespaces
Access Credentials	✅ Full cluster admin credentials	listClusterAdminCredential
2. AKS Data Plane Admin

Description:
This role allows full management of workloads within assigned namespaces but does not allow creating namespaces or managing cluster-level resources.

Scope: Namespace-level (assignable per namespace)

Permissions (JSON example):

{
  "roleName": "AKS Data Plane Admin",
  "description": "Manage all resources within assigned namespaces. Cannot manage cluster-level settings or namespaces.",
  "assignableScopes": ["/subscriptions/<subscription-id>/resourceGroups/<rg>/providers/Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/<cluster>/managedNamespaces/<namespace>"],
  "permissions": [
    {
      "actions": ["Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/managedNamespaces/*"],
      "notActions": [],
      "dataActions": ["Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/*"],
      "notDataActions": [
        "Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/namespaces/*"
      ]
    }
  ]
}


Capabilities:

Resource / Action	Allowed?	Notes
Namespaces	❌	Cannot create or delete
Deployments / Pods	✅	Within assigned namespaces
Services / ConfigMaps / Secrets	✅	Within assigned namespaces
Ingress / StatefulSets / DaemonSets / Jobs / CronJobs	✅	Within assigned namespaces
ResourceQuotas / LimitRanges	✅	Within assigned namespaces
RBAC	❌	Cannot modify roles or bindings
3. AKS Reader Role

Description:
This role provides read-only access to view AKS cluster and namespace resources without modifying them.

Scope: Cluster-level or Namespace-level (depending on assignment)

Permissions (JSON example):

{
  "roleName": "AKS Reader Role",
  "description": "Read-only access to view cluster and namespace resources.",
  "assignableScopes": ["/subscriptions/<subscription-id>/resourceGroups/<rg>/providers/Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/<cluster>"],
  "permissions": [
    {
      "actions": ["Microsoft.Authorization/*/read", "Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups/read"],
      "notActions": [],
      "dataActions": [
        "Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/*/read"
      ],
      "notDataActions": []
    }
  ]
}


Capabilities:

Resource / Action	Allowed?	Notes
Namespaces	✅ Read	Cannot create or delete
Deployments / Pods	✅ Read	Within assigned namespaces
Services / ConfigMaps / Secrets	✅ Read	Cannot modify
Ingress / StatefulSets / DaemonSets / Jobs / CronJobs	✅ Read	Cannot modify
RBAC	❌	Cannot modify roles or bindings
Scope Definition

Roles can be assigned at cluster level (all namespaces) or per namespace.

JSON assignableScopes determines where the role is effective:

"/subscriptions/<subscription-id>/resourceGroups/<rg>/providers/Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/<cluster>"
"/subscriptions/<subscription-id>/resourceGroups/<rg>/providers/Microsoft.ContainerServ
